# Design notes are working research: they weigh other people's software against ours, which is
# exactly what research does and exactly what this project must never publish. They stay on the
# machine of whoever wrote them. The engineering conclusions belong in the code, next to the code.
docs/design/

# Local agent and editor tooling. A launch profile here names paths on one person's machine, and
# this repository is published; nothing in it belongs to the product.
.claude/

# The names the published-text check watches for. Committing a list of other people's products to
# the repository that exists to never discuss them would break the rule it enforces, so the list
# stays local. See the header inside the file.
scripts/guarded-product-names.txt

# Working material for the orchestration build - design notes, same rule as docs/design/.
.orchestration-plan.md

# Isolated worktrees created for parallel agent work; never part of a release.
.claude/worktrees/
